From f8e6e76e176810eb1ec7358f6e4cf59f6d14f593 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 06:59:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Virginia: official portrait, and the Mushore family with
 Shona kinship terms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Hero and directory card use her official profile photograph
  (virginia-portrait-blue-headscarf.jpg). Placeholder alt text removed.

- Her parents added as LIVING family, never as memorial entries:
  Sekuru Johannes Mushore and Ambuya Juliana Mushore. Cards lead with
  the honorific, give the full name and their relation to Virginia, and
  state 'Living' plainly. No death years, no memorial links, no past
  tense anywhere near them.

- Their 72nd anniversary was supplied and then withdrawn by the family.
  Removed entirely — no date, no venue, no time. A comment in data.ts
  records that it must not be reinstated, and that no venue or time for
  living family members should ever be published.

- Shona kinship terms, per the family: Virginia's brothers are Sekuru to
  her children and grandchildren, her sisters are Amaini. Applied to all
  nine siblings and explained in a short note, so the terms read clearly
  to visitors outside the family. Virginia herself carries no kinship
  term — this is her memorial.

- Josephine Mushore's birth year remains blank and labelled 'dates not
  yet recorded'. Still nothing estimated.

Photograph 'virginia-graveside-elders' renamed to
'virginia-parents-at-her-graveside' now that the family has identified
them. Not yet wired; the gallery still awaits the full photo set.
