The five tabs are no longer a John Peters demo — they are the product
structure every memorial receives.

NEW SHARED FRAMEWORK
- src/components/memorialTabs.ts     canonical ids, labels, order, types
- src/components/MemorialTabShell.tsx  the reusable shell: sticky bar,
  ?tab= URL state, sub-navigation, transitions. Renders whatever
  sections a memorial supplies, so a rich memorial and a sparse one get
  the same five rooms.

Tab ids match John Peters' bespoke page exactly, so deep links behave
identically across every memorial and the two remain interchangeable.

VIRGINIA — restructured, NOT reduced
Her ten tabs were redistributed into the five rooms:
  Journey  <- Funeral & Memorial Events, service videos, Anniversary Room
  Memorial <- Overview, Life Story, Gallery, Videos, Voice Notes,
              Guestbook, Digital Candles (sub-nav in the tab bar)
  Glen     <- her resting place at Seke, Zinganga
  Tree     <- parents, siblings, children, grandchildren
  Legacy   <- Living Legacy

Verified by rendering all five rooms: every one of her nine biography
paragraphs, both tribute sets, the corrected hymn, the four-stanza poem,
both scriptures, all gallery captions, the booklets, the timeline, the
twelve candles, the guestbook, the funeral events, the anniversary room,
her parents, all ten siblings with kinship terms, her seven children and
eighteen grandchildren — all still render. Her Happy New Year voice
recording is intact. Nothing was deleted.

DELIBERATELY NOT WRITTEN
- Journey holds a place for the May-October 2025 coordination account.
  It stays empty until the family supplies their own record.
- Glen names Joseph (2024) and Victoria (2016) but invents no burial
  location for either, because none was supplied.

Virginia's old 10-tab bar (virginia/TabBar.tsx) is now unreferenced and
left in place for one release in case the structure needs reverting.
