From 6156d03b023898eb0c2f435996fd2556601c8fea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 07:28:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Virginia: the Journey timeline, and the Chiimba Family
 Glen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

JOURNEY — six stages from the family's own record, May-October 2025.
Passing; coordination; tombstone; the unveiling with its full order of
service; after the service; ongoing remembrance. The Coordinating Team
is named with roles: Rev Chinyowa, Sekuru Robson, Sekuru Joachim
Mushore, and her sons Raymond, Gilbert, Douglas and Hamu.

Three conservative defaults, all reversible:
- WhatsApp handles (South Ray, Giri, Para bellum) are NOT published;
  the family's real names are used instead.
- The photograph album link is NOT published. The gallery holds many
  living relatives at a private gathering, and a public search-indexed
  page would make it findable by anyone. The album is noted as existing
  and held by the family.
- The gap between 19 May and early October is left as a gap. The record
  does not cover a burial date and none was invented.

FAMILY GLEN — Chari Chiimba (1905-1980) and Moses Sarire Ivhu Chiimba
(1943-2001) now rest alongside Virginia, oldest first, each linked to
its own page. Family terms are shown as her children use them
(Grandfather, Uncle) with her own relation beneath (father-in-law,
brother-in-law), since Chiimba is her married name. Joseph and Victoria
Mushore remain 'also remembered' with no burial place invented.

NOT CONVERTED FROM DEMOS. Two clean entries were created instead. Each
demo persona carries nine invented biography paragraphs, six invented
tributes and an invented voice recording; renaming one would have put
fictional content on a real family member. New Memorial flag
 renders a dignified holding page — name, dates,
relation, resting place, and 'This memorial is being written by the
family' — rather than a page of empty section shells.

All 19 demo memorials remain intact and unrenamed.
Everything previously approved is unchanged.
